# Cursor Butler - Local AI for Cursor (CLI)
# Backend: llama.cpp (llama-server) OpenAI-compatible API
# Endpoint: http://127.0.0.1:8080

# Repo contract (must match docs/README.md + docs/README.es.md + docs/AGENTS.md; do not contradict)
# - Docs: docs/README.md; docs/README.es.md; docs/DMAIC.md; AI orchestration: docs/AGENTS.md.
# - Same facts, two README files — no second full doc inside README.md.
# - Official verify: verify.ps1 → ping (test/ping_model.ps1) then test/run_3_programs_and_evaluate.ps1; use -SkipPing to skip ping.
# - test/ = all test assets; Butler smoke/eval at test/*.ps1 except test/legacy/ (historical only).
# - Local parse (no server): scripts/ci_parse_pwsh.ps1 (CI runs the same).
# - Unit gate (no server): scripts/run_unit_tests.ps1 (Pester + stub client; must stay green in CI).
# - Canonical chat binary: cpp/ollama_client.cpp; PS bridge: powershell/ButlerCppBridge.ps1; override BUTLER_CPP_CLIENT.
# - PowerShell integration: powershell/butler_profile.ps1; setup: powershell/setup_butler.ps1.
# - Do not treat Ollama as the default backend in new docs; Butler is llama-server + GGUF.

# AI Provider Configuration
AI_PROVIDER=butler
BUTLER_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:8080
BUTLER_MODEL=local
BUTLER_TIMEOUT_SEC=30

# Timers (use local AI responsibly): si se cuelga ya bye. See https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/ai/overview

# Custom AI Configuration
CUSTOM_AI_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:8080/v1/chat/completions
CUSTOM_AI_MODEL=local
CUSTOM_AI_PROVIDER=butler

# Performance Optimization
GPU_ACCELERATION=true
TEMPERATURE_FAST=0.1
TEMPERATURE_CODE=0.2
TEMPERATURE_GENERAL=0.7
TOKENS_FAST=20
TOKENS_NORMAL=100
TOKENS_CODE=200

# Programming Style Rules
- Prefer clear control flow; allow `else` when it improves readability.
- Validate inputs before parsing or accessing.
- Use `try/catch` around network/file operations; do not swallow errors (rethrow or return a clear failure).
- No verbose answers
- Use readable variable and parameter names (brevity is ok, clarity first).
- No placeholder code
- No unnecessary comments
- No lectures or opinions
- Minimize dependencies
- Flat code structure only

# Butler Best Practices
- Run `verify.ps1` (or `test/run_3_programs_and_evaluate.ps1` with same args) for green/red official check
- Use `test/ping_model.ps1` to verify `llama-server` readiness on `http://127.0.0.1:8080`
- Bounded profile cache: optional env `BUTLER_CACHE_MAX_ENTRIES` (default 1000 in butler_profile.ps1)
- Validate responses automatically
- Cache responses for repeated queries (bounded cache)
- Use GPU acceleration when available
- Optimize prompts for specific use cases